## Coverage scope sentence under review, 24 November 2026

The user questioned the need for the final coverage sentence specifying all 1,332 signings, zero coverage and exact day windows, and suggested equal numbers of missing mentions in each group would reduce its importance. Coverage is not yet approved as a complete subsection.

The purpose of naming zero inclusion is to define the quantity: attention across selected signings, including those with no recorded linked coverage, rather than attention conditional on receiving coverage. Zero counts mean no qualifying linked articles in the collected data, not independently certified absence of any Guardian coverage. Equal absolute numbers of zero counts would represent different proportions in the 88 older / 1,244 younger signings; equal proportions would still not guarantee equal effects on the medians because their positive-count distributions can differ. No equality of zero proportions has been established here, and no new calculation or analysis was undertaken. Do not equate H2 retention with zero-article counts.

For concise Results prose, propose replacing the long scope sentence with "Counts include signings with no recorded coverage." The 1,332-signing population is already introduced, and the exact windows can be specified in Methods. This is a proposal, not an agreed revision; results.tex and the existing agreed evidence wording remain unchanged pending feedback. Source definitions: [agreed coverage subsection](../evidence_and_sources.md#agreed-coverage-results-subsection-24-november-2026), [Methods coverage outline](../evidence_and_sources.md#4-guardian-articles-and-descriptive-coverage), [source completeness limits](../evidence_and_sources.md#closing-reproduction-statement-and-source-status).

Next: settle how much scope information to retain in Results, update the proposed subsection if agreed, then review/approve coverage before sentiment validation. Network/H1 remain approved; Issue 12 is Open and Issue 9.1 deferred/nonblocking. No manuscript prose or analysis was changed during this explanation.

## Zero coverage and sentence sample clarified, 24 November 2026

The user said "okay keep it" after the proposed short zero-inclusion sentence, then asked how a player can have a sentence in the data if no coverage is recorded, suggesting club-only mentions as a possibility. Retained the clarification using the proposed shorter sentence in [results.tex](../results.tex): "Counts include signings with no recorded coverage." The 1,332-signing population is already introduced; exact before/after windows remain in the agreed Methods outline/source definitions. No numbers or coverage calculations changed. Approval of the complete coverage subsection remains pending while clarifying the samples.

Read-only code inspection confirms the distinction:

- [Article counting](../../data/dataset_nlp/sentiment/a1_coverage_age.py), `counts()`: count distinct article IDs after `mentions >= 1`, then reindex to all selected signing IDs and fill absent period counts with zero. A transfer-selected signing can therefore have a count row without any player sentences in that period.
- [Sentence extraction](../../data/dataset_nlp/pipeline/get_guardian_articles.py), `player_sentences()`: retain sentences with a coded player-name match and eligible immediately following He/His sentences. A follow-on sentence requires a preceding named-player sentence; a club-only mention does not itself qualify. The builder derives `mentions` from these named sentences and exports sentences from the same retained list. Retrieved article links with no matched player sentence can remain in metadata, but do not generate sentences for that player or enter the qualifying article count.
- [Sentiment eligibility](../../data/dataset_nlp/sentiment/a1_sentiment.py), `per_signing()`: retain signings with at least five scored sentences in each period, after the main article-type exclusions. A signing with zero qualifying articles in either comparison period cannot qualify on this basis. The accepted H2 result uses 820 signings; coverage retains all 1,332. No sentence is fabricated to represent a zero count. A signing may have sentences on one side and none on the other and still enter coverage counts, but not the paired H2 comparison.

This explanation traces existing code, not a new corpus reconstruction or analysis. Original sentence/score inputs remain unavailable at documented paths and Issue 9.1 remains deferred/nonblocking. Network and H1 prose, approved sample wording, numerical findings and full H1 sensitivity passage remain unchanged. Updated this issue, paper README and tracker; no producer/environment/staging/commit/push changes. **Next:** complete coverage review and make the transition from all-signing article counts to sufficiently covered signing-level sentiment explicit in the next subsection. Issue 12 remains Open; author details and remaining sections are outstanding.

