## Whole-period versus monthly averages, 24 November 2026

The user disliked "We averaged sentence scores within each signing and period, so each signing supplied one before and one after value", asking how a player with five before-period sentences spread across five months contributes to monthly average tone. This identifies a necessary distinction between the H2 statistic and Figure 2's curves; it is not a request for a new analysis.

Read-only source inspection: [per_signing()](../../data/dataset_nlp/sentiment/a1_sentiment.py) groups scores by signing and before/after period and averages all eligible sentence scores in each period; the five-sentence requirement applies to each whole period, not each month. [monthly() and arc()](../../data/dataset_nlp/sentiment/a1_age30_arc.py) independently average within signing-month, then across contributing signings in that age group/month. A signing without scored sentences in a month supplies no signing-month value; there is no zero filling or use of its whole-period mean in that month. The selected [Figure 2 documentation](../../output/h2_monthly_period_means_findings/README.md) confirms changing monthly membership, separate period means and the centred three-month smoothing. The current exporter reads saved smoothed values; the legacy producer's confidence bands are not shown in the approved figure.

For the user's hypothetical one-sentence-in-each-of-five-months example, all five scores enter its whole-before-period average. Before smoothing, each score supplies that signing's value for its corresponding month only; the signing does not contribute a value for other months. Each monthly group average gives equal weight to the signings represented in that month. Subsequent smoothing combines adjacent group-month means, so observed months can influence neighbouring displayed curve values; it does not create new player sentences or a complete player trajectory. Do not imply every signing contributes to every month, equal month weighting in the whole-period calculation, or that H2 is calculated from the smoothed curve.

Replaced the disliked sentence in the proposed [results.tex](../results.tex) subsection with: "For the overall before–after comparison, we averaged all available sentence scores for each signing separately before and after the move. The monthly curves in Figure 2 were calculated separately, using sentence scores from each month." The source uses the agreed Figure 2 label. This is a proposed clarification awaiting review, not approval of the measurement subsection. Explain monthly signing-first/group-second averaging, varying contributors and smoothing when drafting the forthcoming H2 subsection, consistent with the approved caption. The approved network/H1/coverage prose, validation table and figure/caption files are unchanged. Updated issue/checkpoints; no producer, scoring, analysis or environment changes. Next: review the clarification and measurement/validation, then draft H2. Issue 12 remains Open; Issue 9.1 deferred/nonblocking.

