## Guardian club membership clarified, 24 November 2026

The user asked how "Premier League destination membership derived from match fixtures" is obtained. Inspected the existing [Guardian selector](../../data/dataset_nlp/pipeline/get_guardian_articles.py), `season_of()` and `select()`, read-only. It reads `games`, filters `competition_id == "GB1"`, and builds the union of `(season, home_club_id)` and `(season, away_club_id)` pairs. Each transfer is assigned a July–June season from its transfer date; the destination filter retains it only if `(assigned season, to_club_id)` occurs in that union. This is a season-level club-membership criterion, not a requirement for the player to have appeared in a match. It does not use cup fixtures or a fixed present-day list of clubs.

Clarified the proposed [methods.tex](../methods.tex) paragraph by splitting the season conventions into separate sentences and replacing the vague fixture clause with: "A destination club qualified as Premier League if it appeared as a home or away team in a recorded Premier League match that season." This describes the implemented rule without claiming complete historical fixture retrieval. Underlying selection, outputs and sample definitions are unchanged. The standalone loan-return explanation remains removed, as requested.

Updated issue/README/tracker; ran `git diff --check` on changed tracked files. Exact sample paragraphs and approved Results/Discussion, figures/table/captions remain unchanged. No analysis, selector execution, producer, environment change, staging, commit or push. Next: review the clearer provenance/season paragraph, then draft network/backbone Methods. Issue 12 remains Open, contributions explicitly deferred and Issue 9.1 deferred/nonblocking.

## Guardian signing-club terminology clarified, 24 November 2026

The user asked what "destination club" means in the Guardian context. It is the receiving club in the transfer record used to select a signing, i.e. the club the player joined. This metadata check precedes the Guardian article search; it does not identify clubs from newspaper sentences, require the player to appear in a match or define the club most mentioned in the article. In a hypothetical move from club A to club B, club B is the destination/receiving club. No real transfer example or new finding is asserted.

Replaced the final sentence of the proposed [methods.tex](../methods.tex) provenance paragraph with: "For the Guardian sample, the club a player joined had to appear in recorded Premier League matches for the season of the move." This names the selection context and uses plain wording while preserving the previously verified implementation. The whole added paragraph remains proposed; no other prose or selection rule changed. The user's earlier removal of the standalone loan-return explanation is retained.

