## H2 p-value clarified and month-bin detail removed, 24 November 2026

The user questioned whether the empirical equation introduced for one-sided H1 also applies to two-sided H2. Explained that its general "at least as extreme" plus-one form allows either rule, with different tail definitions: H1 uses shuffled gap <= observed gap; H2 uses |shuffled gap| >= |observed gap|. The H1 paragraph's one-sided framing made the proposed cross-reference confusing. Replaced only the H2 p-value sentence with a direct fraction/absolute-value/plus-one explanation. Preserved the exact approved H1 paragraph, assumption and empirical equation. Neither test nor its saved results changed.

